  "method_note": "Population exposure is estimated by projecting WorldPop 100 m (3 arc-sec, 2020, UN-adjusted) grid cell centers onto the 80 m NISAR UTM grid (EPSG:32636) and summing population where cumulative 108-day LOS subsidence is <= -2.0 cm (> 2 cm sinking) and <= -5.0 cm (> 5 cm sinking). Land-cover exposure samples ESA WorldCover 10 m v200 (2021) across the 80 m NISAR grid (0.0064 km^2/pixel) for both the 8-pair common-valid mask (28.66 km^2 <= -2 cm), the final-epoch cumulative mask (49.15 km^2 <= -2 cm), and the <= 2.5 km nearest-neighbor basin interpolation (covering decorrelated center-pivot cropland)."
